libg2c.so is a FORTRAN 77 runtime library provided by GCC. This
distribution of the library is built from GCC 3.4.6, which was the last version
of GCC that provided it.

The GCC 3.4.6 tarball provided in this directory was downloaded from here in
Aug 2021:

https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-3.4/


Build steps
-----------

Run in the current directory:

tar -xf gcc-3.4.6.tar.bz2
cd gcc-3.4.6
patch gcc/unwind-dw2.c ../gcc-3.4.6-unwind-dw2.c.patch
./configure --enable-languages=f77
make
cp x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/libf2c/.libs/libg2c.so.0.0.0 ../x86_64
cp ./x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/32/libf2c/.libs/libg2c.so.0.0.0 ../i386
strip ../x86_64/libg2c.so.0.0.0
strip ../i386/libg2c.so.0.0.0


Notes
-----
- This package replaces the compat-libf2c-34 package that was provided by Red
  Hat in RHEL 7. There is no package in RHEL 8 that provides this library, but
  at least one AWIPS component (GEMPAK) still requires it.
- The patch file gcc-3.4.6-unwind-dw2.c.patch is provided by the Raytheon
  AWIPS team, to enable this old version of GCC to be built using RHEL 8's
  distribution of GCC.
- The library has been prebuilt to avoid long build times. Even just the
  FORTRAN 77 component of GCC takes a while to build, and we only need a small
  piece of that.
- Both 32-bit and 64-bit versions of libg2c.so are provided in this
  package, though it's not clear whether both are still used in AWIPS
  as of this writing (Aug 2021)


